   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>To free the memory, you have to do the exact opposite of what you did when allocating the memory.</p>\n\n<p>Start with the dynamic elements which you have created insid the loop:</p>\n\n<pre><code>for (int i = 0; i &lt; n_samp; i++){\n    free( *(m+i) );\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>and then do the rest:</p>\n\n<pre><code>free( m );\nfree( sol );\n</code></pre>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 77477018,
   "parent_id": 45256601,
   "parent_type": "question",
   "author_user_id": 892256,
   "author_display_name": "Ed Heal",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/45256601/#comment77477018_45256601",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2017-07-22T16:23:26Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "you are doing the loop after free <code>m</code>. wrong way around"
